  "note": "A Bn two up withdrawing by night (IC s91-93 pp 481-491; IBB s72-76 pp 366-386). The click is the Bn HQ of the old posn; the aim is the direction of withdrawal, the second click the new main posn (planned). Rear parties (a Pl of each forward Coy with part of the weapon section, IC p 488) hold to the time of abandonment; Coy RVs where the Pls gather, the Bn checkpoint and Bn RV on the routes back (IC s92 paras 7-8 pp 486-487); Coy embussing points 1500-2000 m behind the old posn on the Coy routes (IBB s75 para 19 p 383), the Bn EP behind the Bn RV with a covering Pl of the depth Coys (IBB p 379); the intermediate posn, a Coy group (IBB p 379), far enough back that he must move his field artillery first (IBB s74 para 4 e p 373: his 105 mm IFG 17.2 km, ORBAT) and behind an obstacle if there is one (IC p 482); part of the artillery repositioned 5000-6000 m back from the old gun area, taken at the Bn rear (IBB s76 para 5 p 385). The programme from last light follows IBB s75 para 11 pp 379-380. Battle Posns are drawn turned to face the enemy behind the plan.",
